### Manual tests for User Account stories #6-10
### Needs: VS Code "REST Client" extension, and the backend running (npm run dev:server).
### Click "Send Request" above each request, top to bottom.
### This uses the SHARED database. Only suspend or edit the test account you create in step 2.

@base = http://localhost:3000/api
@origin = http://localhost:5173

### 1. Log in as a User Admin (saves the session cookie automatically)
# @name login
POST {{base}}/login
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "username": "admin1", "password": "password123" }

@csrf = {{login.response.body.csrfToken}}

### 2. #6 Create a test account. profileId 3 is Customer in the seeded data.
###    If unsure, run step 5 first and read the profileId next to a Customer account.
# @name created
POST {{base}}/user-accounts
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "username": "kaz.test",
  "password": "test-password-123",
  "name": "Kaz Test",
  "email": "kaz.test@example.com",
  "profileId": 3
}

@newId = {{created.response.body.id}}

### 3. #6 Create again with the same user ID -> expect 409 "already in use"
POST {{base}}/user-accounts
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "username": "kaz.test",
  "password": "test-password-123",
  "name": "Duplicate",
  "email": "other@example.com",
  "profileId": 3
}

### 4. #6 Create with bad fields -> expect 400 with a list of errors
POST {{base}}/user-accounts
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "username": "x", "password": "short", "name": "", "email": "nope", "profileId": 999 }

### 5. #10 Search all accounts
GET {{base}}/user-accounts

### 6. #10 Search by keyword
GET {{base}}/user-accounts?keyword=kaz

### 7. #7 View the test account
GET {{base}}/user-accounts/{{newId}}

### 8. #7 View an account that does not exist -> expect 404
GET {{base}}/user-accounts/999999

### 9. #8 Update the test account's name
PUT {{base}}/user-accounts/{{newId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "name": "Kaz Test Renamed" }

### 10. #9 Suspend the test account
POST {{base}}/user-accounts/{{newId}}/suspend
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### 11. #9 Try to log in as the suspended account -> expect 403 "This account is suspended."
POST {{base}}/login
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "username": "kaz.test", "password": "test-password-123" }

### 12. #8 Reactivate the suspended test account (Update with status "active")
PUT {{base}}/user-accounts/{{newId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "status": "active" }

### 13. #8 Update cannot suspend -> expect 400 "Use Suspend to suspend an account."
PUT {{base}}/user-accounts/{{newId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "status": "suspended" }

### 14. Log in as the reactivated account -> expect 200
POST {{base}}/login
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "username": "kaz.test", "password": "test-password-123" }
